<p>Kuwaiti authorities said an Iranian strike hit a service building at a power generation and water desalination facility in Kuwait, killing an Indian worker and causing significant material damage. India’s embassy in Kuwait confirmed the death and said it was in touch with Kuwaiti authorities and the worker’s employer. Live coverage from NDTV and Al Jazeera linked the Kuwait incident to a broader regional escalation involving Iranian retaliatory attacks and ongoing strikes on Iran by the United States and Israel. NDTV’s live updates said more than 3,000 people have been killed.</p><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Critical utility: The strike damaged infrastructure tied to both electricity generation and desalinated water supply, highlighting risks to essential civilian services in a region where desalination is central to daily life.</li><li>Embassy response: The Indian mission said it was coordinating with local authorities and the employer after the worker’s death, signaling immediate consular involvement for the victim’s case.</li><li>War toll: NDTV’s live updates said more than 3,000 people have been killed, placing the Kuwait incident within a much larger regional escalation.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Kuwaiti authorities: Officials said the Iranian attack struck a service building at the power and desalination plant, killed one worker and caused significant material damage. (<a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/3/30/iranian-attack-damages-kuwait-power-and-desalination-plant-kills-worker'>Al Jazeera</a>)</li><li>Indian Embassy in Kuwait: The embassy confirmed the worker’s death and said it was engaging with Kuwaiti authorities and the employer following the strike. (<a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/iran-israel-us-war-updates-live-march-30-2026/article70801564.ece'>The Hindu</a>)</li><li>NDTV live coverage: Its reporting framed the Kuwait strike as part of Iran’s wider retaliatory attacks during ongoing US and Israeli strikes